shape theory.emergence.composition : theory.emergence, theory.emergence.effective-contact {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 6.2 (Emergent Composition).
// When two shapes A and B are in bilateral contact (each in contact
// with the other, both contacts effective) the coupled system is
// itself a shape. It has:
//   - Prior configuration: the character of A and B and their
//     reference relations
//   - Emergent configuration: produced by their coupled transformation
//   - Its own structure S_D, derived from the coupling geometry
//   - Character that neither A nor B has individually
//
// The emergent shape's structure is not chosen. It is derived from
// the coupling. Different coupling geometries yield different
// emergent structures.
//
// Emergence produces genuinely new character. The emergent shape has
// structural properties that are not properties of the components.
// They are properties of the coupling geometry.
//
// Derives from: theory.emergence, theory.emergence.effective-contact
  """
}
